      "message": "According to VT-d spec: \"This register is treated as RsvdZ by implementations reporting Performance Monitoring (PMS) as not\nsupported in the Extended Capability register.\"\n\nso we should validate these registers in the ecap_pms\u003d0 case as well (i.e. validate that they are zero in this case), and not just here (and first of all not here) but in pkvm_iommu_mmio_write(), and not just PERFINTRADDR/PERFINTRUADDR but PERFINTRDATA/PERFINTRCTL as well?\n\nDon\u0027t know, maybe something like this (for all 4 registers)?\n\n```\n--- a/drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu.c\n+++ b/drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu.c\n@@ -645,8 +645,12 @@ int pkvm_iommu_mmio_write(u64 phys, int len, u64 val)\n                        }\n                }\n                break;\n-       case DMAR_FEADDR_REG:\n        case DMAR_PERFINTRADDR_REG:\n+               /* RsvdZ if no PMU support */\n+               if (!ecap_pms(iommu-\u003eecap) \u0026\u0026 val)\n+                       ret \u003d -EINVAL;\n+               fallthrough;\n+       case DMAR_FEADDR_REG:\n                /*\n                 * FEADDR/PERFINTADDR holds the MSI destination address.\n                 * The IOMMU writes to this address when a fault occurs, bypassing\n```\n\n...As for these checks of FEADDR/FEUADDR and PERFINTRADDR/PERFINTRUADDR here in iommu_init(), I\u0027m not sure we need them at all. If we really want to sanitize _initial_ values of _physical_ IOMMU registers during pKVM initialization, why these specific registers only?",
